{"name":"Twilightcore","title":"Twilightcore","revision":235718,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Twilightcore","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"heading","text":"History"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"During the COVID-19 pandemic of Autumn 2021, the app TikTok experienced a Twilight renaissance. This was due to the release of Midnight Sun in 2020 and people wanting an escape from current events."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Nostalgia is only one of the factors that ushered in Twilightcore. With 2000s fashion making a return, Netflix introducing the Twilight franchise to their platform at the time, the weather progressing into winter, and the aforementioned nostalgia coincided perfectly and created what it is now known as Twilightcore."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Twilightcore uses muted colors and dark hues to mimic the cinematography of the Twilight films, more specifically the first one. The aesthetic is meant to have romanticized overcast scenes and desaturated clothing. It is usually based in suburban neighborhoods and schools or deep in forests. The fashion for Twilightcore is based on the Twilight series and the Vampire Diaries series."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"list","text":"Muted colors such as greys, greens, reds, blues"},{"kind":"list","text":"Light jackets in dark colors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Long-sleeved shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wide-leg or flare dark jeans"},{"kind":"list","text":"Slip-on sneakers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Warm form-fitting clothing"},{"kind":"list","text":"Layered outfits"},{"kind":"list","text":"Black dresses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Flannel shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gold necklaces/lockets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chokers"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Activities"},{"kind":"list","text":"Reading (Bella Swan and Violet Harmon)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Writing in a diary (Elena Gilbert)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Going to high school night football games (Elena Gilbert)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cheerleading (Elena Gilbert)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Listening to music (Violet Harmon)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"TV Series"},{"kind":"list","text":"American Horror Story (2011-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Supernatural (2005-2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Vampire Diaries (2009-2017)"},{"kind":"list","text":"True Blood (2008-2014)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Movies"},{"kind":"list","text":"Thirteen (2003)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Twilight (2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Twilight Saga: New Moon (2009)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Twilight Saga: Eclipse (2010)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn - Part 1 (2011)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn - Part 2 (2012)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Books"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Twilight Saga"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Artists"},{"kind":"list","text":"Arctic Monkeys"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ashbury Heights"},{"kind":"list","text":"bôa"},{"kind":"list","text":"Calla"},{"kind":"list","text":"Current Joys"},{"kind":"list","text":"Deftones"},{"kind":"list","text":"Evanescence"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hannah Peel"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hole"},{"kind":"list","text":"Imogen Heap"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mazzy Star"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mitski"},{"kind":"list","text":"Muse"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nirvana"},{"kind":"list","text":"Phoebe Bridgers"},{"kind":"list","text":"PinkPantheress"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pixies"},{"kind":"list","text":"Poppy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ramones"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Cure"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Doors"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Smiths/Morrissey"},{"kind":"list","text":"Strawberry Guy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Suki Waterhouse"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Albums"},{"kind":"list","text":"Everybody Else Is Doing It, So Why Can't We? by The Cranberries"},{"kind":"list","text":"Louder Than Bombs by The Smiths"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mellon Collie And The Infinite Sadness by The Smashing Pumpkins"},{"kind":"list","text":"Punisher by Phoebe Bridgers"},{"kind":"list","text":"So Tonight That I Might See by Mazzy Star"},{"kind":"list","text":"Twilight by bôa"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fallen by Evanescence"},{"kind":"list","text":"Saturday Night Wrists by deftones."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Songs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Duvet by bôa"},{"kind":"list","text":"Twilight by bôa"},{"kind":"list","text":"All The Things She Said by t.A.T.u"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Perfect Girl by Mareux"},{"kind":"list","text":"Oh Klahoma by Jack Stauber"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bring Me To Life by Evanescence"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lovesong by The Cure"},{"kind":"list","text":"A Forest by The Cure"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pet Sematary by Ramones"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Killing Moon by Echo and the Bunnymen"},{"kind":"list","text":"People Are Strange by The Doors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Your Face by Wisp"},{"kind":"list","text":"Мало by Акула"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Resources"},{"kind":"list","text":"I like boys who sparkle (Tumblr)"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/35/Dark_Y2K_aesthetic_mood_board.jpeg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20230413052425","caption":"Dark Y2K aesthetic mood board","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Dark_Y2K_aesthetic_mood_board.jpeg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/1046-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/43/Twilight_Forest.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20211225213055","caption":"Twilightcore · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Twilight_Forest.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/1046-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}